criteria:
Inclusion Criteria:

* Rhegmatogenous retinal detachment with single retinal break, or group of breaks within 1 clock hour of one another, located in the inferior 4 clock hours;
* Retinal break(s) anterior to the equator of the globe;
* Macula detached;
* Ocular media judged to be sufficiently clear for adequate examination and laser retinopexy;
* Age 18 years or older; and
* Participant is capable of signing informed consent or has an acceptable substitute decision maker capable of signing the informed consent form on their behalf. A responsible parent or caregiver of an assenting minor must agree with the minor's decision to participate.

Exclusion Criteria:

* Age younger than 18 years;
* History of prior ocular surgery in the study eye, excluding laser refractive surgery, uncomplicated cataract surgery and pneumatic retinopexy;
* History of active uveitis or uncontrolled glaucoma (IOP \> 35) in the last 3 months;
* Presence of proliferative vitreoretinopathy Grade C or higher;
* Presence of choroidal detachment on baseline clinical examination or B-scan ultrasound
* Has a medical condition requiring use of anti-coagulant medication
* Patient or caregiver unable to provide informed consent;
* Patient unwilling to return for research follow-up visits; or
* Known allergy to nickel or ocular viscoelastic device.
